{
 "about": "How legacy reads the url of a GENERAL PIP. Each PIP answers a marker from the route its url reaches, and the condition compares the PIP with the marker a reading predicts: `subject.<pip> == resource.want OR resource.a == 'y'`. When no route answers, or the url fails the call, the PIP fails and a-y is false too. A backslash in the url: routes for the path without it and with it. ${resource.u} with a plain value: round 28 saw every url with ${resource.…} fail without a call, but each of its values held a character a URL reserves. A single quote without a space: round 28 asked one only beside spaces.",
 "resourceTypePrefix": "PARITY_SUITE_R29U_",
